# A build context is not a repository. `.gitignore` keeps these out of git; it
# does nothing for `docker build`, which copies whatever is in this directory
# unless told otherwise — and an image is pushed to a registry.
#
# `probe-output/` is the one that matters: it holds raw and masked output from
# real calls, including call identifiers. It is kept out of git deliberately
# and must stay out of any image for the same reason.
probe-output/
docs/video/
.env
.env.*

node_modules/
dist/
.git/
.github/

# Test and tooling surface the running console never reads.
test/
coverage/
*.log
